Going forward: Lauren designs in Figma first, then we match the site to Figma. Do not silently push site-only tweaks back into Figma unless she asks.

Same token names can have different values on desktop vs mobile. Apply the value for the breakpoint you are implementing.

Code breakpoints for this site:

- Full nav: `lg` (1030px and up)
- Desktop type and header chrome (logo size, hero type, heading sizes): `md` (768px and up), including tablet with hamburger
- Mobile type and header chrome: below 768px, from the 400 mobile frame

Keep the current menu overlay behavior (clear on hero, blurred bar after companies). Do not revert those.

Hero top padding is not the Figma section token. The header overlays the hero, so match the gap **under the nav** (see the figma-homepage-updates skill). Bottom padding is independent. Do not mix `md:pt-*` with `lg:py-*` on the hero inner box.

If the user points at a mismatch, read that section’s node. Do not guess which section they mean.

**Approved code exceptions** (do not revert to Figma `-02` without asking Lauren):

- Cropped photos fill their frames with `object-cover` (no stretching), even when Figma exported width/height percentages.
- Header overlay behavior: clear over the hero on the homepage frames; solid (`ink` 80% + blur 50px + shadows) is a separate Figma state (`Header Desktop-02 — Solid (after Companies)`), not applied to the default overlay menu.
